telecom giant Huawei Technologies has  long been at the center of drama between  the US and China but what exactly is  Huawei and why is the company so  significant here's what you need to know  first and foremost Huawei is a global  telecom behemoth it sold roughly 52  million smartphones in the last quarter  nearly seven million more than Apple it  employs 180,000 people more people than  Intel and it generated more than 92  billion dollars in revenue last year  that's more than twice that of Facebook  you might not use huawei products  because they aren't readily available in  the US and some other Western countries  regardless the company is the largest  maker of telecom equipment including  things like switches routers and cell  tower gear Huawei also sells personal  computers and a wide array of wireless  devices like smart watches and it's the  second largest smartphone company after  Samsung in China the company is seen as  the country's biggest global success  story so why is Huawei so important to  the u.s. it's all about competition not  only is the telecom giant a rival of  major Western companies but Huawei is  also seen as a global leader in 5g the  ultra-fast wireless technology that will  soon be connected to everything that's  good for China and bad for the US  Washington worries that if Huawei wins  the race to develop 5g technology  Americans could one day be forced to buy  equipment from the company and right now  no US companies are seen as major  competitors in this area the biggest  contenders are Sweden's Ericsson and  Finland Nokia but that's not all Huawei  is also seen as a cybersecurity threat  to the US Washington has accused the  company of being a potential conduit for  Chinese spying and cyber theft because  the company is so big and because it's  technology is used all over the world  the u.s. worries that Beijing could  force the company to engage in fair  activities like crippling communications  infrastructure remotely controlling or  destroying telecom gear or even spying  on America and its allies for its part  qua Way says its products are completely  safe and that the company does not do  any bidding for the Chinese government
 

